  "notes": "The northern Jordan River Crossing has two parallel prestressed concrete decks with separate roadbeds, cast piers, chamfered girders and steel parapets. The model fits the mapped bend and joins both terminals’ approach lanes. The model depicts the present paired Sheikh Hussein crossing near Beit She’an and Irbid. Terminal structures, the old historic bridge and the unrelated Damia crossing to the south are outside the asset. Both deck centrelines and approach connections follow PMTiles and the aerial view. The prestressed girder shape, piers, parapets, dimensions across each deck and deck elevations are reconstructed from exterior photographs and standard Terrarium. The applicable source is the modeled crossing itself. The downstream road feature carries the Damia name in this PMTiles snapshot, but the two traces form this same northern crossing.",
